# Project Charter
## Sales Activity Tracking System

### 1. Project Overview
The Sales Activity Tracking System is designed to help sales teams and management monitor sales activities, customer visits, business opportunities, and follow-up actions through a centralized platform.

### 2. Business Background
Sales activities are essential for maintaining customer relationships and generating new business opportunities.

However, without a centralized monitoring system, management may face difficulties tracking sales visits, evaluating sales performance, monitoring follow-up activities, and obtaining accurate sales activity reports.

This project aims to improve sales activity visibility, accountability, and reporting efficiency.

### 3. Project Objectives
- Centralize sales activity records.
- Monitor customer visits and meeting outcomes.
- Improve follow-up activity monitoring.
- Provide management with sales activity reports.
- Improve sales team productivity and accountability.

### 4. Project Scope

**In Scope**
- Sales employee login.
- Customer visit planning and recording.
- Customer visit activity reporting.
- Meeting outcome documentation.
- Follow-up activity tracking.
- Sales activity dashboard.
- Management reporting.

**Out of Scope**
- Sales commission calculation.
- Invoice and payment processing.
- Inventory management.
- Full CRM implementation.

### 5. Key Stakeholders
- Project Sponsor
- Sales Manager
- Sales Supervisor
- Sales Representatives
- IT Project Manager
- Business Analyst
- System Analyst
- Development Team
- IT Support Team

### 6. Expected Deliverables
- Project Charter
- Business Requirement Document (BRD)
- Functional Requirement Specification (FRS)
- As-Is and To-Be Business Process
- System Flow Diagram
- System Design Documentation
- Project Plan
- Test Scenarios and UAT Documentation

### 7. Success Criteria
- Sales representatives can record customer visits.
- Sales managers can monitor sales activities.
- Follow-up activities can be tracked.
- Management can access consolidated sales activity reports.
- Manual reporting activities are reduced.

### 8. Project Assumptions
- Sales representatives have access to the system.
- Customer information is available and maintained.
- Management defines the required sales activity indicators.
- The project is developed as a simulated portfolio case.

### 9. Project Constraints
- Limited project resources and development time.
- User adoption and training requirements.
- Data accuracy depends on timely user input.

### 10. Project Disclaimer
This is a simulated portfolio project created for professional demonstration and learning purposes. All business scenarios, requirements, and data are fictional.
